- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests`

**How to implement.** A material version holds one of the three crystal-parameter records as its physics, beside the complexity tree, and composes its engine properties through the S10.1 builders; the editor, the facets and the entry-file schema follow (the S11.1 brief 'Material physics form'; .spec-md §3.16). The editor follows as it followed the published gyration law (step 10): the ladder edits complexity trees, so a crystal entry opens view-only; a crystal material reaches the library through its entry file (import and drop, S3.1-S3.2) and through Promote to library (S11.5). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) `CrystalPhysics.fs` (step 353), after the three records: `CrystalParameters` = `UniaxialCrystal of UniaxialParameters` | `TriclinicCrystal of TriclinicParameters` | `AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal of AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`, with `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` (each case its record's `opticalProperties`) and `member this.toProperties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp`, `this.opticalProperties.dispersive` (`Dispersion.fs`, `OpticalProperties.dispersive`): the same tensors at every wavelength. It is stored in the serializer's case form, as `SlotTurn` is (step 256), so no int tag is added. (2) `MaterialLibrary.fs`: `MaterialPhysics` (step 354) gains `CrystalParameterPhysics of crystal : CrystalParameters`, and `toProperties` answers `crystal.toProperties` for it. (3) Each shared member gains its arm. `LibraryFacets.fs`: `type CrystalParameters with member this.anisotropy : Anisotropy` (`Uniaxial` for `UniaxialCrystal`, `Biaxial` for the two triclinic cases) and `member this.transparency : Transparency` (`Transparent` for the uniaxial and the triclinic crystal, `Absorbing` for the absorbing one), and `MaterialPhysics.anisotropy` answers the crystal's. `MaterialComplexityEditor.fs`: `editableComplexityOpt` answers `None`. `NkDispersionChart.fs`: `gyrationComponents` answers `allGyrationComponents` and `muKind` `ScalarMuKind`, μ being the vacuum's in every builder. So `initMaterialEditor` opens a crystal entry as `ViewOnlyMaterial` with step 354's caption, its preview charting `shown.toProperties`, and the Materials window offers no Edit for it, with no change to either view. (4) `LibraryFacets.fs`: the private `constantEpsOpt`, `dispersiveEpsOpt`, `activeOpt` and `magneticOpt` answer `None` for a crystal, and the transparency facet extracts `crystal.transparency` for it; the dispersion facet already reads `MaterialEntry.dispersion`, which is `ConstantMaterial` for a crystal; the dispersion-model, gyration-class, handedness and magnetic facets do not apply, because they classify the ladder's value trees and a crystal's gyration is parameters. `OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs`: `ofEntry` answers no defined segment for a crystal, so it never flags, as a constant complexity does not. (5) Entry files. `LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `LibraryEntryPayload` (step 25) gains `CrystalMaterialPayload of CrystalParameters`, whose `kind` is `MaterialEntryKind`; `ofMaterialEntry` writes it for a crystal and `MaterialPayload` for a complexity; `toMaterialEntry` reads either; every other decoder answers `EntryKindMismatchErr` for it as for `MaterialPayload`, and every other complete match over the payload gains the case. `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-material.schema.json` (step 30): under version 1 the payload's case tag is `MaterialPayload` or `CrystalMaterialPayload`, written as the schema writes the existing tag, the crystal inside it bound by the serializer (`MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one). The schema version stays 1: no stored file changes, because every existing material keeps `MaterialPayload` (.spec-md §7: no migration, no stored data predates the case). The database stores the canonical payload (step 69), so nothing else in Storage changes. No editor for crystal parameters, no wire tag and no other member is added. (6) Tests, over test-local records written as literals (a uniaxial crystal n_o 1.544, n_e 1.553, g11 3.0e-5, g33 −1.0e-5; a triclinic one; an absorbing triclinic one with fifteen distinct values). `MaterialComplexityTests`: `a crystal-parameter material composes its record's engine properties at every wavelength`: for each case an entry of `CrystalParameterPhysics` answers, at 400, 600 and 800 nm, `properties.getProperties` equal to its record's `opticalProperties` (ε, μ and ρ through the file's tolerance helpers, 1e-15) and `dispersion` `ConstantMaterial`; `a crystal-parameter physics offers no editable complexity, so its entry opens view-only`: a crystal answers `editableComplexityOpt = None` and a constant isotropic complexity `Some` of itself. `LibraryFacetsTests`: `a crystal-parameter material classifies its anisotropy and transparency from its crystal, and the ladder's facets do not apply`, over entries built as `materialEntryWith` builds them, with a crystal physics:anisotropy `Uniaxial` / `Biaxial` / `Biaxial`, transparency `Transparent` / `Transparent` / `Absorbing`, dispersion `Constant`, and the dispersion-model, gyration-class, handedness and magnetic facets not applicable. `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`: `a crystal-parameter material never flags out of band`: a wavelength sweep over 300-900 nm flags nothing for a crystal entry. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`: `a crystal-parameter material's builder and decoder are inverse`: `ofMaterialEntry` then `toMaterialEntry` answers each crystal entry, its content's payload being `CrystalMaterialPayload`, and `toSample` of it `EntryKindMismatchErr`. `EntryFileJsonTests`: `a crystal-parameter material entry file round-trips each crystal record`: each crystal content goes `sealed`, `fileText`, `parseEntry MaterialEntryKind` and answers an equal envelope whose decoder answers the entry, the text naming `CrystalMaterialPayload`. `MaterialProxyTests` (`MaterialProxyContract`, steps 66, 69, so both stores run it): `a crystal-parameter material is stored and resolved at its version by its physics`: a minted absorbing crystal material saved through `saveMaterial` resolves at version 1 to an equal entry and is listed by `listMaterials ActiveOnly`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`: `a crystal-parameter entry opens the editor view-only and previews its crystal's properties`: `initMaterialEditor` over a uniaxial crystal entry gives `ViewOnlyMaterial`, its `previewProperties.getProperties` at 600 nm equal to the crystal's `opticalProperties`, and its `previewGyrationComponents` equal to `allGyrationComponents`.

**Acceptance.** After the crystal case lands, an entry of `CrystalParameterPhysics` MUST compose its record's builder at every wavelength, classify by its crystal's anisotropy and transparency, never flag out of band, open view-only, and round-trip its entry file as `CrystalMaterialPayload` while every existing file keeps its bytes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a crystal-parameter material composes its record's engine properties at every wavelength`, `a crystal-parameter physics offers no editable complexity, so its entry opens view-only`, `a crystal-parameter material classifies its anisotropy and transparency from its crystal, and the ladder's facets do not apply`, `a crystal-parameter material never flags out of band`, `a crystal-parameter material's builder and decoder are inverse`, `a crystal-parameter material entry file round-trips each crystal record` and `a crystal-parameter material is stored and resolved at its version by its physics` under `MaterialProxyTests` and `MaterialProxySqliteTests`, the count rising by 8; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a crystal-parameter entry opens the editor view-only and previews its crystal's properties`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.
